      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is Yan Qing, the same young East Asian man with the same face, black hair, small scar above the outer end of his left eyebrow and plain dark clothes. In Picture 1 he stands beside the loaded e-bike at frame left. He mounts it carefully and rides forward away from the pork counter into the market aisle, staying on the customer side and moving deeper into the frame.\n<Subject 2> is the same stocky middle-aged butcher in the navy work shirt and worn brown apron. He stays behind the counter on frame right, watches the departure and does not follow or cross the counter.\n<Subject 3> is the same dark blue-black electric bicycle from Picture 1. Preserve its exact step-through shape, headlamp, handlebar, seat, wheels and screen direction. The bicycle begins parked, then moves only forward into the aisle.\n<Subject 4> is the one kraft-paper-wrapped pork parcel, secured flat behind the seat on the rear rack with the same plain dark strap. It stays attached and does not shift, multiply, open or fall.\n<Picture 1> is the actual final frame of the preceding loading shot and fixes the exact opening pose, camera, bike orientation, parcel, characters, stall and lighting.\n\nsummary:\nContinue from the exact previous end frame in one static shot. Yan Qing mounts the loaded e-bike and rides straight away from the stall into the market aisle. The butcher remains behind his counter. The same wrapped pork stays secured on the rear rack.\n\nretention_analysis:\nThis is a continuous same-camera handoff from Picture 1, not a new angle. Preserve the exact crop, perspective, lamp row, door, counter, aisle, character positions and dawn lighting. Yan Qing remains on frame left/customer side. The butcher stays on frame right/vendor side. The e-bike and one strapped parcel remain unchanged. Only Yan Qing, the bicycle and the bicycle wheels move forward; no reverse, turn-back, teleport, cut or camera movement.\n\ndetailed_description:\nPhotorealistic live-action drama matching Picture 1. Fixed medium-wide camera from the same market aisle viewpoint; realistic practical warm stall lamps and faint cool dawn ambience. Maintain natural movement and human/bicycle proportions. The departure should feel like an ordinary quiet early-morning errand, not a product demonstration.\n\nOne uninterrupted 7.29-second action:\n0.0-1.3s Yan Qing turns the handlebars slightly toward the open aisle and mounts the e-bike in one careful motion. The loaded parcel remains flat and strapped behind the seat.\n1.3-2.2s He settles, grips the handlebars and starts the motor gently. The bicycle rolls forward; no wheel spin while stationary.\n2.2-6.3s Yan Qing rides straight away from the pork stall down the open aisle, keeping to the left-side route and moving deeper into the market. The camera and vendor remain fixed.\n6.3-7.29s The bicycle recedes toward the market mouth, still carrying the same parcel. End with the rider moving away, not stopping or turning back. The butcher remains at his stall.\n\nNo subtitles, captions, logos, readable signs or watermarks. No added dialogue is needed for this visual shot; audio is not being evaluated. No change of face, clothing, bike design or parcel. No extra parcel, no lost cargo, no abrupt speed burst, no camera pan/zoom, no cross-axis movement, no duplicate person, no advertising composition, no cartoon or flat 3D look.",
